# Drives `149_self_ending_match` ([LLOG.15.1], [IRET.12.2]). `flip`
# fires in the first pump over A(x, enter) and K(x); its first emit replaces the
# A it matched, so its match ends there, and neither that new A(x, leave) nor
# the C(x) it emits next is justified: both are retracted as they are made. The
# Probe in the second pump would let `a_live` or `c_live` fire on a survivor.
# `verify tms` judges both pumps on both legs.
assert A id=x kind=enter
assert K target=x
pump
assert Probe n=1
pump
